import GUT.SU6.SelectionRules.FinalNoGoAssembly

/-!
# Axiom audit for the conditional final assembly

This reusable audit covers only the scoped theorem actually formalized here:

* a differentiable injective matrix embedding and its actual hypercharge
  circle construct the semisimple embedding classification weak-doublet decomposition and the unique physical
  centralizer cocharacter pair;
* an actual injective oriented centralizer circle has the flipped or standard
  integer pair;
* the supplied flipped SM-plus-singlets trace certificate is impossible by
  the independent `swap36` restricted-character obstruction;
* the surviving standard coefficient certificate yields standard charge-orbit bridge and then Abelian proton-operator neutrality for
  an arbitrary ordinary Abelian residual group;
* alternatively, the hypercharge character rigidity physical-torus character theorem selects the standard
  pair directly for the same strict ordinary source, without using the flipped route or a
  neutral-block premise;
* the strongest interface obtains both that hypercharge character rigidity input and the later standard charge-orbit bridge input
  from one local charge-resolved physical-torus coefficient certificate;
* a mass-index interface obtains that same coefficient certificate from an
  actual equivariant mass map and a single character-level statement of the
  exact low-energy chiral spectrum, without choosing kernel/cokernel
  equivalences;
* a structural alternative constructs the ultraviolet signed Hilbert spaces
  from the actual charged source and obtains that same coefficient certificate
  from an equivariant mass map plus kernel/cokernel representation
  equivalences;
* a stronger normal-form interface constructs the mass map and those two
  equivalences from unitary light-plus-heavy decompositions with a shared
  paired heavy representation;
* the result specializes directly to finite Abelian residual groups;
* each main route constructs a supported, physically admissible standard
  dimension-six local operator class with trivial residual character, without
  assuming a nonzero Wilson coefficient or decay amplitude;
* the dynamical premise that at least one gauge-mediated channel is present is
  used only by the optional stronger present-channel corollaries.

It does not upgrade a merely continuous embedding to differentiability,
construct the light-plus-heavy decomposition from an arbitrary Lagrangian, or
derive a nonzero coefficient or channel presence.  None of those dynamical
claims is needed for the selection-rule target audited here.
-/

